s  and I had no control over my anger my  emotions my spending anything my words I  was mean I you know I was just an ugly  person few more years go by and we hit a  breaking point in their relationship  where I just saw no hope scared to death  you know what what that meant to our  daughter I finally gave up and hired an  attorney and file for divorce and and I  left  [Music]  we met together at some you know kind of  mandatory counseling thing I think and  somehow we walked out of the place  different doors or something and we met  on on the stairs or something outside of  this counselor's office and that was a  that was a bit of a turning point in our  relationship  we knew we loved each other we were like  we don't want to be doing that so we  started counseling in April of 2012 a  friend of mine asked me if I wanted to  go see Dave Ramsey at a live event here  in San Antonio and it was the most  amazing experience it she said that that  line that he says if you have problem  with your money it's not the money it's  a person in the mirror and right there  it just clicked I was the problem it  gave me hope that I could change the  person in the mirror and that we could  get together on our finances and we  could still still you know make our  marriage work I knew I could do this and  all I had to do was convince him  ask him can we do this you know can we  try this please and really you didn't  trust me talk is cheap right actions  speak much louder than words and by this  time we're starting to go to a local  church lo and behold our our church  offers Financial Peace University so  simultaneously we signed up for a  marriage recovery class and for FPU and  it just gave us a lot of tools to to  really diffuse these these difficult  situations that all couples go through  for us were buried in over $300,000 in  debt when we went through that class and  what I saw and Maddy was this incredible  energy to do whatever it takes to get  out of debt she's we sold every